{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_STD_SECTION_1_Returned_by_AUTOSAR_Services_to_indicate_a","src":"manifest","doc":"SWS_RTE","page":586,"text":"1 Returned by AUTOSAR Services to indicate a\ngeneric application error.\nImmediate Infrastructure Error codes\nRTE_E_COM_STOPPED\n128\n[SWS_Rte_01060]\nRTE_E_TIMEOUT\n129\n[SWS_Rte_01064]\nRTE_E_LIMIT\n130\n[SWS_Rte_01317]\nRTE_E_NO_DATA\n131\n[SWS_Rte_01061]\nRTE_E_TRANSMIT_ACK\n132\n[SWS_Rte_01065]\nRTE_E_NEVER_RECEIVED\n133\n[SWS_Rte_07384]\nRTE_E_UNCONNECTED\n134\n[SWS_Rte_07655]\nRTE_E_IN_EXCLUSIVE_AREA\n135\n[SWS_Rte_02739]\nRTE_E_SEG_FAULT\n136\n[SWS_Rte_02757]\nRTE_E_OUT_OF_RANGE\n137\n[SWS_Rte_08065]\nRTE_E_SERIALIZATION_\nERROR, RTE_E_HARD_TRANSFORMER_\nERROR\n138\n[SWS_Rte_08725]\nRTE_E_SERIALIZATION_\nLIMIT, RTE_E_TRANSFORMER_\nLIMIT\n139\n[SWS_Rte_08726]\nRTE_E_SOFT_TRANSFORMER_\nERROR\n140\n[SWS_Rte_08551]\nRTE_E_COM_BUSY\n141\n[SWS_Rte_01389]\nRTE_E_RAM_UNCHANGED\n142\n[SWS_Rte_04582]\nOverlayed Errors\nThese errors do not refer to the data returned with the API. They can be overlayed\nwith other Application- or Immediate Infrastructure Errors.\nRTE_E_LOST_DATA\n64\n[SWS_Rte_02571]\nRTE_E_MAX_AGE_EXCEEDED\n64\n[SWS_Rte_02702]\nTable 5.5: RTE Error and Status values\n⌋(SRS_Rte_00051)\nThe underlying type for Std_ReturnType is defined as a uint8 for reasons of com-\npatibility – it avoids RTEs from different vendors assuming a different size if an enum\nwas the underlying type. Consequently, #define is used to declare the error values:\n1\ntypedef uint8 Std_ReturnType;\n2\n3\n#define RTE_E_OK 0U\n[SWS_Rte_01269] ⌈The standard errors as defined in [SWS_Rte_07712] including\nRTE_E_OK shall be defined in the RTE Header File.⌋(SRS_Rte_00","caption":"1 Returned by AUTOSAR Services to indicate a","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_STD_SECTION_1_Returned_by_AUTOSAR_Services_to_indicate_a","releases":["R23-11"],"page":586,"hash":"8a35743d54e2cb5f","caption":""}],"releases":["R23-11"],"kind":"snippet","platform":"classic","targ